<h1>Interaction Legend</h1>
<p>
    Map navigation often goes undiscovered.
    <code>MapInteractionMetadata</code> exposes MapLibre's default shortcuts and
    gestures to allow consumers to visualise them in their UI.
</p>

<h2 id="reference_only">// reference_only</h2>
<p>The metadata is descriptive only, it does not enable configuring shortcuts and gestures.</p>
<p>
    Pass the same
    <code>CooperativeGestures</code> value to the map and
    <code>GetDefaults</code>.
    Cooperative mode replaces ordinary scrolling, one-finger pan, and two-finger pitch with the intentional gestures shown in the guide.
    This is to allow scrolling through the page without getting locked onto the map.
</p>

<h2 id="example">// example</h2>
<p>
    This example shows how one could use and visualise the shortcuts and gestures.
</p>

<ExampleView TComponent="InteractionMetadataExample" AdditionalSources="@([typeof(InteractionGestureVisual)])">
    <InteractionMetadataExample />
</ExampleView>
